jitStopT -- SEQ 384 R1 (Tony, 2026-10-19): stop() in a jitted body ends the run AT RUN TIME, not at build.
Today stop() and the cerr before it run at BUILD time: the run prints "SPJ ran n 0" and exits inside the compile.
Intended: "SPJ ran n 1" (the fire's value) and then exit, = the interpreted twin jitStopIT. The body cannot fire
